<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John III, Duke of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1374–1425</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as John the Pitiless, John of Bavaria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John III, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, called the Pitiless, was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>-elect of Liège, where he crushed a rebellion in 1408. After the death of his brother William in 1417 he fought his niece Jacqueline of Hainaut for the inheritance of Holland, Zeeland and Hainaut. His death in 1425 opened the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> to take these lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-iii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="John III, Duke of Bavaria" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siegel_Johann_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
